  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Code Memory for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "**Give your coding agent the relevant source before its first step.** Code Memory (CM) is a local code index and context plugin for JavaScript and TypeScript projects. It combines symbol lookup, dependency graphs, and semantic search to reduce repeated source discovery.\n\n**Unofficial community project.** Independently developed; not affiliated with or endorsed by DeepSeek."
    },
    {
      "section": "Code Memory for DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "**English** · [Русский](README.ru.md) · [Download v0.9.3](https://github.com/kobubu/Rag-Coding/releases/tag/v0.9.3) · [Windows installation](docs/INSTALL-WINDOWS.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "- Supplies compact source context before the first model call in DeepSeek Harness.\n- Looks up named files and symbols directly; uses local MiniLM embeddings and LanceDB when discovery is needed.\n- Expands relevant dependencies using the TypeScript compiler's symbol and call graph.\n- Checks source versions and avoids repeating unchanged whole files already supplied to Harness.\n- Exposes an MCP server for Codex and Claude Code and an optional `UserPromptSubmit` hook for automatic context.\n- Includes CM Atlas, a local map of modules, symbols, and their relationships."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "The index, embeddings, and graph stay on your computer. Selected code is still sent to your model provider when you use a cloud model. CM does not include model credits or a model-provider subscription.\n\nActual CM Atlas screenshot of this repository's public `src` directory: 39 modules, 2,409 symbols, and 8,321 relationships. The current Atlas interface is in Russian; the installation guide below is in English."
    },
    {
      "section": "Measured results, with limits",
      "text": "The published Harness pilot used GPT-6 Luna on **six task types in one repository**, Geo Dash. Three evaluation series each ran 36 sessions: no CM, the earlier CM, and the newer CM, with two repeats per task and arm."
    },
    {
      "section": "Measured results, with limits",
      "text": "| Newer CM versus no CM | Published result |\n|---|---:|\n| Total model tokens | 45–66% fewer across the three series |\n| Estimated model price | 30–47% lower |\n| Total Harness session time | 18–37% lower |\n| Independently checked solutions, pooled across series | 36/36 with newer CM; 35/36 without CM |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Measured results, with limits",
      "text": "These are **small, single-project pilot results**, not guaranteed savings. The ranges are observed series results, not confidence intervals. Costs are estimates; session time does not include first-time installation or indexing. All attempts, including failures, are retained. Earlier approaches and native-client experiments have different outcomes; do not transfer these percentages to every client or workload."
    },
    {
      "section": "Codex and Claude Code",
      "text": "In Codex and Claude Code, CM adds its context through a `UserPromptSubmit` hook served by a warm local daemon; the installer configures it. Fourteen tasks in the same repository — the six above plus eight new ones that CM was not tuned on — three repeats per task and arm, 84 sessions per client:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Codex and Claude Code",
      "text": "| CM versus no CM | Codex, GPT-6 Luna | Claude Code, Sonnet 5.5 |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Independently checked solutions | 41/42 vs 40/42 | 42/42 vs 42/42 |\n| Total model tokens | 58.0% fewer | 40.4% fewer |\n| Estimated / reported price | 29.0% lower | 18.0% lower |\n| Total session time | 35.9% lower | 35.1% lower |\n| Median session | 7.3 s vs 12.2 s | 12.4 s vs 18.7 s |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Codex and Claude Code",
      "text": "In both clients the paired 95% bootstrap intervals for tokens and time exclude zero. Three larger tasks — a feature across three modules, a rename across imports, a new parameter in several places — also gain: Codex 60.1% fewer tokens and 39.2% less time, Claude Code 35.0% and 16.4%. One weak spot is documented: on a rewrite of a counting function, agents with CM more often lose a key-coercion detail and need a second edit. Two unrelated public libraries that CM was not tuned on, six tasks each, confirm the effect: node-semver — Codex 59.1% fewer tokens and 49.0% less time, Claude Code 38.2% and 18.0%; superstruct (TypeScript) — Codex 39.2% and 27.4%, Claude Code 28.6% and 12.0%, with an 8.3% lower price. Three projects are still not a guarantee for other workloads. The MCP server alone, without the hook, showed no savings."
    },
    {
      "section": "Codex and Claude Code",
      "text": "[Method, raw results, and reproduction](docs/EFFICIENCY-AB.md) · [Codex and Claude Code experiments](docs/NATIVE-CLIENTS.md) · [What did not work](docs/HISTORY.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install into an existing Harness",
      "text": "Requires DeepSeek Harness **0.2.0-rc.2** and Node.js 24 or 22.19+ within 22.x:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:kobubu/Rag-Coding#v0.9.3\n```\n\nThe tag contains the compiled plugin, CLI entry points, and Atlas. CM needs no installation build or Vite/React runtime modules. Then [prepare the project index and local model](docs/DEEPSEEK-PLUGIN.md#github-installation). A ready release tarball is also available:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install into an existing Harness",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/kobubu/Rag-Coding/releases/download/v0.9.3/dsh-plugin-code-memory-0.9.3.tgz\n```\n\nGit tags before 0.9.1 require their release tarball or an explicit source build. The new runtime works with scripts disabled; native dependencies follow the host package manager's policy."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install into an existing Harness",
      "text": "If CM was installed with the Windows bootstrap, update it using the new ZIP and the same `-InstallRoot`. Harness 0.2.0-rc.2 can prefer a CM copy beside its own installation over a profile-installed copy; adding another Git dependency to that older installation does not replace its launcher or embedded copy. The bootstrap creates a new release directory and switches managed project launchers."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install on Windows",
